WEBVTT

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:20.490
You, a piddly little Nehalem, are standing 
up to my, Juggernaut Maximum's, attacks?!

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.500
Too bad for you.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:29.850
The next attack, for sure!

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.310
If you get that chance, that is.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:33.270
But you no longer have a way to win!

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:34.490
Say what?!

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.340
I will ride to the next grade!

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.560
Ride! The Vanguard!

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:49.660
Descend, Dragonic Overlord!

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:52.610
Impossible!

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:41.510
I win.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:46.350
Juggernaut Maximum lost? Man, 
I've got such crappy luck!

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:47.650
Luck?

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:50.340
Damn it all!

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:51.430
Morikawa...

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:54.840
Just as freakishly good 
as always, I see, Kai.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:56.690
Miwa?

00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:00.220
Have you had a winning streak 
ever since you came back here?

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:01.850
Yeah, guess so.

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:03.090
You go, dude.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:07.580
Hey, shop girl! Any of the 
regulars better than this guy?

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:10.370
I don't have a clue.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:13.220
No clue? Then it's decided!

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:15.900
Toshiki Kai is the best player in this store!

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:19.590
Hey, you! That's not what "no clue" means!

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.590
Shut up, loser!

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:24.050
Say that again, you...

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.050
Morikawa...

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:26.790
What? I called you a loser, loser.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:29.320
Shut it! Things just didn't 
go my way today, is all.

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:29.930
Yeah, right...

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.820
That's all it takes to be the best?

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:36.890
This level doesn't get me fired up at all.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.840
How boring...

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:42.930
Aren't there any strong players around here?

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:50.580
Vanguard of Destiny!

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:56.730
With hundreds of millions of people 
around the world playing card games,

00:03:56.730 --> 00:04:00.880
they've naturally become 
a part of our daily lives.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:09.030
Cardfight! Vanguard is the card game 
that gets most of our attention now.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:15.130
And one of those cards let 
me meet him once again.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:19.340
Hitsue Middle School

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:20.200
And finally the battles of 
Kawanakajima reach their climax!

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.610
Finally, the final battle!

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:25.540
In this one, Uesugi has 
forces numbering 12000!

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:28.230
Announce a battle formation 
called the "Wheel Winding"!

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:31.150
Sneak up to Shingen's main 
force under the cover of fog!

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:34.210
His opponent: Takeda's forces number 8000!

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.520
Announce a battle formation called 
the "Crane's Wing" and fight back!

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.820
But they're outnumbered!

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:41.310
Takeda's forces are in trouble!

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:44.610
His class is always so over-the-top...

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:46.600
With the battle upon him, Shingen 
ends up losing his younger brother,

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:47.530
He's not Japanese, but he's such a 
maniac about the Sengoku period...

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.190
and after the battle both 
forces are exhausted.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:48.720
What a weirdo.

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:54.050
And so, in this Sengoku 
period of shrewd tactics...

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:55.740
Let me see here...

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:59.180
You! How would you survive, Aichi Sendou?

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.150
Yes?

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:05.400
What would you do to leave your 
mark on the Sengoku period?

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:09.060
Uh... Um...

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:10.910
What's the matter, Aichi?

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.130
Haven't heard your voice in, like, forever!

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:15.640
You can't get any quieter than this guy!

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.010
What's the matter, Sendou?

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:19.000
Image! Form an image in your mind!

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:25.940
I-I... I would make sure I always 
had a line of retreat behind me.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:32.120
Man, what a coward!

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:34.100
He's, like, king of the wimps!

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.640
What a dope, as usual!

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.760
I mean, you can't get more small fry 
than him. No, he's just perfect!

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:45.810
Sendou, that might be a good way to 
survive during the Sengoku period,

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:50.370
but why don't you try imagining 
yourself with a slightly bigger role.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.530
I-I'm sorry...

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:55.830
Man, I screwed up big time...

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:59.400
Now then, this battle at Kawanakajima

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.380
caused him to lose his chance to 
take control of the government...

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:06.590
But there's no way that I could appear 
alongside all these amazing warriors!

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:12.840
Oh, I know. I bet that he could 
even be in the Sengoku period.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:16.430
The Vanguard warrior, Blaster Blade!

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.480
Who the hell are you?

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:24.250
I am Blaster Blade!

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:26.940
I have come from the United Sanctuary!

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:29.750
Are you some kind of damned monster?

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:31.450
Prepare yourself, fiend!

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:34.010
I will take you on!

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:43.130
It's no use...

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:46.980
There's no card in this pack 
strong enough to beat that guy!

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.880
Do I just suck that bad?

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:52.090
Damn you, Toshiki Kai!

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:55.640
I was always the best player at that store!

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:59.610
To lose against some punk who just moved 
into town... I won't let this stand!

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:03.260
I've got to get a card powerful 
enough to defeat him somehow!

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:07.730
What's that small fry doing 
with a grin on his face?

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:12.200
Wait, that's... a Vanguard card!

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.780
And it's Blaster Blade!

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:18.170
That's a legendary, powerful, rare card!

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.920
W-What is it, Morikawa?

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:33.760
Aichi Sendou... I didn't know 
that you were a Vanguard Fighter.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.530
A Vanguard Fighter?

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:38.380
Don't play dumb.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:41.980
Anyone who fights with Vanguard 
cards is a Vanguard Fighter.

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.600
You're one too, right?

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:45.110
No, you've got it wrong.

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:49.000
After all, I've never played a cardfight.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:51.900
I'm not a Vanguard Fighter or anything.

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:57.680
Fine, whatever. Then show me the 
card you have hidden in your pocket!

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:06.140
Seriously! It's actually Blaster Blade!

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:08.540
With this I can totally beat that guy!

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:10.730
Ooh, let me see!

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:12.480
Whoa, awesome!

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:14.580
I'm taking this guy straight to the shop!

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:16.460
Wait, Morikawa!

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:17.620
Don't take it from me!

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:21.440
I got that card from someone 
special! It's important to me!

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:22.480
Wait!

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:27.910
Shut up already. You're not 
a Vanguard Fighter, right?

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.960
I feel sorry for this card, 
never getting to fight.

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:34.480
So I'll take it off your hands.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.700
Okay, let's get to Card Capital!

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:37.450
Yeah!

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:43.410
G-Give it back... Give me back my card...

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:55.330
Kai! You and me, now!

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:56.930
You're that guy from yesterday...

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:59.400
Oh sure, talk big after beating me once!

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:02.880
We'll fight once again to decide once 
and for all who the best in this shop is!

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:04.420
I don't want to.

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:05.770
What?

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:07.920
You suck at Vanguard.

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:10.940
Your fighting techniques are simplistic 
and your strategy has no depth.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:13.390
You rely too much on the 
cards' brute strength.

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:18.020
I won't get anything out of 
fighting you. So I won't.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:20.090
Dude, that's harsh!

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:23.320
Won't get anything, huh?

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:26.370
Then if you win, I'll give you this card!

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:28.840
Ooh! That's Blaster Blade!

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:31.760
How rare! I didn't realize 
anyone still had one.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:33.170
Blaster Blade?

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:34.680
It couldn't be <i>that</i> card, right?

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:36.800
So, what'll it be?

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:37.840
Fine.

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:40.050
It's on.

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:46.140
My... My card...

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:51.900
Damn it, why? Why is my luck so bad?

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:54.410
It's not your luck. It's your skill.

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:56.780
Ride the Vanguard!

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:03.660
I'm pretty sure this is the 
shop that Morikawa mentioned...

00:10:06.350 --> 00:10:09.180
That's 6 damage. I win.

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:12.530
T-This shouldn't be!

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:15.070
And that's a wrap.

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:16.860
Here, it's yours.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:20.290
Blaster Blade...

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:23.300
What? You don't seem so interested...

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:25.400
G-Give me my card back.

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:26.580
Who's this?

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:28.210
Aichi...

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:30.350
Morikawa, please!

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:32.060
It's very important to me!

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:34.450
Don't look at me!

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:36.740
Your card? You mean this one?

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:41.080
Yes, yes! That's mine!

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:43.700
Please give it back.

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:45.800
Why should I?

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:47.750
This card is now mine.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:02.840
Hey...

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:05.390
U-Uh...

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:13.880
To we Vanguard Fighters, nothing is more 
sacred than the results of a fight.

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:17.930
This guy challenged me to a fight 
by betting this card, and lost.

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:21.850
But it's mine...

00:11:21.850 --> 00:11:25.780
A card that is lost in a Vanguard fight can 
only be taken back by a Vanguard fight.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:30.930
T-Then, will you fight me?

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:38.640
Sure, I'm game.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:41.300
Hold it! What are you saying, Aichi?

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.910
I thought you'd never played 
a Vanguard fight before?

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:45.560
You don't even have a deck, right?

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:47.560
I've never played before,

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:53.140
but I've always wanted to, so I made a deck.

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:54.160
Seriously?

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:57.340
You're on. Sit over there.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:00.650
Time for losers to get lost!

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:05.840
What are you lookin' at?

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:07.050
Same as you.

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:11.950
This is a fight between someone who has never played 
Vanguard before and the strongest player in the store!

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:13.460
This is gonna be hilarious!

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:16.300
No, he's not the best yet!

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:17.590
Today was just a fluke...

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:26.170
Since you are a beginner, I will 
explain the rules as we play.

00:12:26.170 --> 00:12:26.550
Okay.

00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:33.070
And before we begin, your deck won't be 
complete without this Blaster Blade, yes?

00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:34.630
Yes, that's right.

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:36.510
Fine, you can borrow it.

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:38.970
That should be a decent handicap for me.

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:40.880
Blaster Blade...

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:42.560
T-Thank you!

00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:47.220
You're not just explaining the rules, 
but lending a card to your opponent?

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:49.410
It's rare to see you act nice.

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:52.130
That's not the case.

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:55.820
I'll only explain the rules 
once. Listen carefully.

00:12:55.820 --> 00:12:56.740
We're beginning.

00:12:56.740 --> 00:12:57.630
Right.

00:12:58.280 --> 00:12:59.630
Picture it in your mind...

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:06.900
The two of us have appeared on a planet 
similar to Earth called Cray, in spirit form.

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:12.470
There are only two powers 
given to us weak forms...

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:19.040
One power, called "call", is to summon the 
creatures that live on this planet, called "units".

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:23.330
The units we can summon 
are the ones in our deck.

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:26.930
First, we each draw five cards from our deck.

00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:31.090
These are the units which we can summon.

00:13:34.090 --> 00:13:37.330
Each card has its own grade and ability cost.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:40.830
The units' various abilities 
are also written.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:45.340
And then there is the 
second power we are given:

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:49.950
the ability to possess units 
with our spirits, called "ride".

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:51.000
Oh, I see.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:51.940
Dude...

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:55.730
The units that we possess 
are called our "Vanguards".

00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:59.790
The word means "the one leading us forward".

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:01.410
Vanguard...

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:02.950
The one that leads...

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:09.110
Now, the games starts as we become 
Vanguards on the planet Cray.

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:13.270
That card you chose to lay 
down is a grade 0 unit, right?

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:14.210
Yes.

00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:15.790
Good. Turn it over.

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:19.450
Ready? Stand up the Vanguard!

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:21.130
Lizard Runner Undeux!

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:23.080
For me...

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:26.880
Stardust Trumpeter! Stand up!

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:34.600
Now we are both standing on 
the planet Cray as Vanguards.

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:38.350
Is it okay if I take the first turn? 
That'll make explaining easier.

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:39.810
Sure.

00:14:40.510 --> 00:14:42.940
First, I draw a card.

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:48.110
Now I can possess a unit one grade 
higher than the current Vanguard.

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:51.200
Stack a unit on top of the Vanguard!

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:54.280
Ride the Embodiment of Armor, Bahr!

00:14:55.710 --> 00:15:01.140
At the same time, you can call units with 
a grade the same or lower than your Vanguard.

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:03.700
These units are called the "rear-guard".

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:06.200
I call the Hope of Flame, Aermo!

00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:15.820
With this, I have two units on the field.

00:15:15.820 --> 00:15:17.470
And with them, I attack!

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:22.180
Although the player that goes 
first can't on their first turn.

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:25.320
That ends my turn.

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:27.270
It's your turn now.

00:15:27.270 --> 00:15:28.140
Right.

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:29.320
I'll draw a card...

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:34.270
Then, I'll ride the Little Sage, Marron!

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:38.110
A-And call Wingal, too!

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:46.330
Now we both have two units on the field.

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:47.710
Will you attack?

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.260
I-I'll attack!

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:51.800
Okay, good.

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:53.970
Then announce it and put 
the Vanguard to rest.

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:57.180
I attack Bahr with my Vanguard, Marron!

00:15:57.180 --> 00:16:02.440
When you attack, your Vanguard receives 
power from the rear-guard unit behind it.

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:07.480
In that case, attack together with 
the power of the rear-guard, Wingal!

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:15.670
Then, when you attack, you draw the top card 
from your deck to check for a drive trigger.

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:20.120
Is there a mark on the 
upper right of the card?

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:22.550
If not, then just add it to your hand.

00:16:22.550 --> 00:16:24.920
So the attack was a success?

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:26.330
Yes.

00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:29.170
All right...

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:32.500
Your attack hit my Vanguard.

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:34.180
This is the damage from that hit...

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:42.230
When I get a total of six damage, my 
spirit vanishes from the planet Cray.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:45.410
In other words, I lose. Understand?

00:16:45.410 --> 00:16:46.410
Right...

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:49.250
Good. This time it's my turn. Here I go.

00:16:50.080 --> 00:16:52.430
Ride the Dragon Knight Nehalem!

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:55.030
Call Bahr!

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:04.130
Looks like he's finally getting serious.

00:17:04.390 --> 00:17:06.920
Aichi's gonna get his butt whipped good.

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:12.880
I attack Marron with Bahr!

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:17.940
Um... Bahr's power is 8000, and 
Marron's power is 8000, so...

00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:20.350
If the powers are equal, then 
the attack goes through.

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:28.180
Then if Nehalem attacks after I get 
hit by Marron, I'll take two damage?

00:17:28.550 --> 00:17:33.440
However, you can weaken your opponent's 
attack by using the cards in your hand.

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:34.690
In that case...

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:37.700
I guard with the Bringer of Good Luck, Epona!

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:41.450
The number written vertically 
becomes your defense power.

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:45.200
Bahr's power disappears because 
of your shield of 10000.

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:47.270
The attack is ineffective.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:50.920
After the attack, the card 
you used to guard is retired.

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:57.980
Now I attack Marron with Nehalem 
combined with Aermo's power!

00:17:58.900 --> 00:18:01.020
I don't guard.

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:04.210
Then I check for a drive trigger.

00:18:11.220 --> 00:18:13.070
Now, it's your turn.

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:14.050
Right.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:17.950
We both have 1 damage each.

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:18.970
Okay!

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:21.430
Ride the Knight of Silence, Gallatin!

00:18:25.770 --> 00:18:28.730
Plus, I call Marron and Flogal!

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:33.460
I combine Wingal's power with 
Gallatin and attack Nehalem!

00:18:36.730 --> 00:18:41.780
Then I combine Flogal's power 
with Marron and attack Nehalem!

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:44.060
I can't let you do that.

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:47.410
Your attack cannot get through!

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:51.060
In that case, my turn is over.

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:54.070
B-But I did cause 1 damage.

00:18:54.710 --> 00:18:59.430
If we continue doing 1 damage to each 
other, I'll be the one to win first!

00:18:59.980 --> 00:19:01.740
What are you so relieved about?

00:19:02.650 --> 00:19:05.920
Did you seriously think I was just 
going to let it end this way?

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:08.610
It's about time I ended this lesson.

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:12.640
I call Wyvern Strike Tejas and Jarran!

00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:19.510
Picture the attack I'm about to begin...

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:23.640
First I attack Gallatin with Bahr!

00:19:24.520 --> 00:19:26.140
I guard with Flogal!

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:32.650
Next, I combine Jarran's power 
with Tejas and attack Gallatin!

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:36.770
Two Wyverns?

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:41.990
That's right! And when Jarran supports 
Tejas, he gets an additional 4000 power!

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:53.620
Now we both have 2 damage, so it's tied.

00:19:53.620 --> 00:19:56.780
But I still have an attack left.

00:19:56.780 --> 00:20:00.090
I attack Gallatin with 
Nehalem supported by Aermo!

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:02.770
That's 16000 power...

00:20:02.770 --> 00:20:04.590
But that's not all.

00:20:07.460 --> 00:20:10.810
It's the Embodiment of the Spear, Tahr; 
however, what's important is this here!

00:20:12.220 --> 00:20:14.850
When this mark appears on the card you draw,

00:20:15.390 --> 00:20:21.570
your attack power increases by 5000 and 
the damage you can do goes up by 1!

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:24.160
Then, that means...

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:28.570
If this attack hits, you take 2 damage!

00:20:48.370 --> 00:20:49.480
Are you okay?

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:54.340
Two cards, just like that...

00:20:54.340 --> 00:20:56.230
Four damage before I even knew it.

00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:58.110
This is... This is...

00:20:58.410 --> 00:21:00.400
You were able to picture it, I see.

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:02.690
Yes, this is Vanguard!

00:21:06.470 --> 00:21:08.110
I guess this is over.

00:21:08.880 --> 00:21:11.410
Oh, I could totally still make a comeback.

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:12.370
You got that right!

00:21:14.350 --> 00:21:16.480
Now, it's your turn.

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:27.640
What's the matter? Have you 
lost the will to fight?

00:21:31.290 --> 00:21:32.390
Aichi?

00:21:33.470 --> 00:21:36.000
You're amazing, just as I figured.

00:21:36.590 --> 00:21:38.530
But this is fun, Kai!

00:21:42.600 --> 00:21:45.140
How do you know Kai's name?

00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:48.930
It was my dream to be able to 
fight with you like this, Kai.

00:21:49.650 --> 00:21:51.070
Just as I thought.

00:21:51.070 --> 00:21:54.310
You are Aichi Sendou.

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:56.360
That's right, Kai.

00:21:56.600 --> 00:22:00.460
And this is the power that 
you gave me back then.

00:22:01.510 --> 00:22:02.460
I see.

00:22:03.160 --> 00:22:04.340
Here we go...

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:06.960
Stand up, my avatar!

00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:08.220
Ride!

00:22:12.590 --> 00:22:14.900
Blaster Blade!

00:23:50.750 --> 00:23:53.030
Kai, I knew you'd be amazing.

00:23:53.030 --> 00:23:54.270
But, this is fun!

00:23:54.270 --> 00:23:56.370
You're Aichi Sendou...

00:23:56.370 --> 00:23:58.240
You guys know each other?

00:23:59.410 --> 00:24:01.410
The one who gave me this Blaster Blade...

00:24:01.410 --> 00:24:04.790
And the one who made me think of 
becoming a Vanguard Fighter...

00:24:04.790 --> 00:24:07.170
The person who started it all?

00:24:07.170 --> 00:24:08.550
Are we finished talking now?

00:24:08.950 --> 00:24:13.100
On the next Cardfight! 
Vanguard: Ride to Victory!

00:24:13.100 --> 00:24:15.690
Now, whenever you're ready, Aichi!

00:24:16.030 --> 00:24:19.440
Picture our Vanguard Fight in your mind!
